This could also have some interesting implications for theology as well. I
have heard it argued (from a Christian perspective) that the distinction
between "natural" and "supernatural" is artificial; that when God performs a
miracle (also *makfa* according to the definition), he is simply
manipulating the universe in an atypical manner (he did after all, create
it), which we can already do to a lesser extent with technology.
           
